From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SenkOS
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 21:31:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: h616: add the video engine (Cedrus)

The H616/H700 has the H6's Cedar video engine at 0x1c0e000. Interrupt
(SPI 93) is from the Anbernic BSP device tree. Like the upstream v3
series (Chen-Yu Tsai, linux-sunxi 2026-07), the engine uses two IOMMU
masters (3 and 2) and needs both the VE SRAM and SRAM C; with master 2
missing, part of its DMA bypassed translation and frames came out empty. The H6 variant
of the cedrus driver matches through the fallback compatible: MPEG-2,
H.264, H.265 (8/10-bit) and VP8 decoding.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616.dtsi | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616.dtsi
index 4dd356159..4284fafae 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616.dtsi
@@ -619,6 +619,19 @@ gic: interrupt-controller@3021000 {
 			#interrupt-cells = <3>;
 		};
 
+		video-codec@1c0e000 {
+			compatible = "allwinner,sun50i-h616-video-engine",
+				     "allwinner,sun50i-h6-video-engine";
+			reg = <0x01c0e000 0x2000>;
+			clocks = <&ccu CLK_BUS_VE>, <&ccu CLK_VE>,
+				 <&ccu CLK_MBUS_VE>;
+			clock-names = "ahb", "mod", "ram";
+			resets = <&ccu RST_BUS_VE>;
+			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 93 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+			allwinner,sram = <&ve_sram 1>, <&sram_c 1>;
+			iommus = <&iommu 3>, <&iommu 2>;
+		};
+
 		iommu: iommu@30f0000 {
 			compatible = "allwinner,sun50i-h616-iommu";
 			reg = <0x030f0000 0x10000>;
-- 
